Port Flutter's iOS UITextInput editing fixes into gpui_ios.

Ported from flutter/flutter engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/darwin/ios/framework/Source/FlutterTextInputPlugin.mm
@ 3.50.1 (ae9b586f34a8443573f82ef57c3bf914a908cbf7). Copyright 2014 The Flutter Authors. BSD-3-Clause.

What, each with the Flutter test (patch 0028's table) that failed before it:
- `deleteBackward` deletes one character, not a whole grapheme cluster, unless that is an emoji (Flutter's Thai rule,
  flutter/flutter#24203, #21745, #39399; `IsEmoji` asks the system ICU). Flutter deletes one UTF-16 unit; GPUI's text
  is a Rust string, so this deletes one code point (both halves of a surrogate pair). testDeletingBackward.
- the iOS 16 workaround for flutter/flutter#111494: `deleteBackward` keeps the emoji it deleted, and an `insertText:`
  of just that emoji's first UTF-16 unit inserts the whole emoji; `shouldChangeTextInRange:replacementText:` (new,
  returns YES) clears it. testSystemOnlyAddingPartialComposedCharacter, testCachedComposedCharacterClearedAtKeyboardInteraction.
- UIKit's strings reach GPUI through UTF-16, with half a surrogate pair as U+FFFD. Before, `to_string()` read a NULL
  `UTF8String` for such a string: undefined behaviour, an abort in debug builds. Not in Flutter, whose text is an
  NSString.
- `textInRange:` clamps the range to the document ("Sanitize the range to prevent going out of bounds"): UIKit keeps
  ranges across app edits. It returned nil. testTextInRange.
- `unmarkText` with no marked text leaves the app alone (Flutter's early return); it called `unmark_text`.
  testUITextInputAvoidUnnecessaryUndateEditingClientCalls.
- `tokenizer` is `GPUITextInputTokenizer`, Flutter's `FlutterTokenizer`: line granularity from the text's line breaks,
  since the default `UITextInputStringTokenizer` does not handle it (asked for the line at 15 of
  "how are you\nI am fine, Thank you" it answered 14..17). testFlutterTokenizerCanParseLines.

Why: these are the failures Flutter's tests found in upstream's UITextInput view; each fix is Flutter's.

Test: patch 0028's rows, on the iOS simulator (`scripts/ios-text-oracle.sh` in Parallax).

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

